# VTID-03609 — commands run, in order, with what each proves.
# Run from services/gateway/ unless noted.

# 1. Typecheck. Clean apart from four pre-existing missing OPTIONAL deps in this
#    local checkout (@aws-sdk/client-ecs, @aws-sdk/client-polly, pg, compression);
#    CI's npm ci installs them.
npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json

# 2. The suite carrying the 5 new VTID-03609 tests, run ALONE and read in full.
#    This matters: an earlier run of this same suite was reported as passing when
#    it had in fact failed to LOAD (ReferenceError: readFileSync is not defined).
#    A suite that fails to load emits no per-test failure lines, so a grep for
#    '✕' showed nothing and the other suites' passing count was mistaken for
#    success. CI caught it. The command below prints every test name.
npx jest test/orb/live/characterization/vertex-wake-opener-v2.characterization.test.ts
#  -> 10 passed, including all 5 under
#     "VTID-03609: the sync new-day branch awaits greetingFactsReady"

# 3. Both affected suites together — outputs/jest-affected-suites.txt
npx jest test/orb/live/characterization test/services/conversation/compute-greeting-decision.golden.test.ts
#  -> 235 tests passed, 35 snapshots passed, 0 failed tests.
#     3 suites fail to LOAD locally on "Cannot find module '@aws-sdk/client-polly'"
#     (system-instruction, time-since, tool-catalog characterization). That is this
#     checkout's incomplete node_modules, not a repo state, and it is unrelated to
#     this diff — those three do not import anything this PR touches.

# 4. No stale VTID reference survives — outputs/grep-no-stale-vtid.txt
#    (run from the repo root)
grep -rn "VTID-03593" services/gateway/src services/gateway/test
#  -> no matches (exit 1)

# 5. The touched router still serves — outputs/curl-orb-live-transport.txt
curl -s -w '\n%{http_code} %{content_type}\n' https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/orb/live/transport
#  -> {"ok":true,"transport":"sse"} / 200 application/json; charset=utf-8

